From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GE-Proton <git@localhost>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 03:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winepulse: Route Sony Direct profile through PipeWire

PipeWire's Default Sony controller profile publishes the four-channel raw
PCM as a hidden split parent and identifies it through api.alsa.split.name.
The Direct profile instead publishes that same four-channel PCM as its public
Direct__Direct__sink and does not provide a split parent.

The Windows Sony audio path consequently failed to resolve a PipeWire target
in Direct mode and fell back to opening api.alsa.path (hw:Control) directly.
That stole the PCM from PipeWire, removed and recreated the Direct endpoint,
and invalidated the application's controller audio and haptic streams.

Treat a four-channel Sony Direct sink as its own raw PipeWire target.  The
existing PipeWire ALSA plugin path can then retain PipeWire as hardware owner
in both profiles: Default continues to use its hidden split parent, while
Direct uses its public four-channel node.  Do not change or persist the
user-selected card profile.
---
 dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c b/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
--- a/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
+++ b/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
@@ -1560,6 +1560,17 @@ static void pulse_add_device(struct list *list, EDataFlow flow, pa_proplist *pro
             if ((dev->raw_haptic_target = malloc(target_len)))
                 memcpy(dev->raw_haptic_target, target, target_len);
         }
+        else if (strstr(pulse_name, "Direct__Direct__sink") &&
+                (channel_mask & KSAUDIO_SPEAKER_QUAD) == KSAUDIO_SPEAKER_QUAD)
+        {
+            size_t target_len = strlen(pulse_name) + 1;
+
+            /* The Direct profile exposes the physical four-channel PCM as
+             * this public PipeWire node rather than as a hidden split parent.
+             * Use the real Pulse name, not Wine's generated endpoint id. */
+            if ((dev->raw_haptic_target = malloc(target_len)))
+                memcpy(dev->raw_haptic_target, pulse_name, target_len);
+        }
         if (alsa_path && alsa_path[0])
         {
             size_t alsa_path_len = strlen(alsa_path) + 1;
-- 
